From 8d086207c6323e1175ab5577dcee19493cbc819c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cedric Hauber <hauber.c@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:47:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(heater): turn spools whose filament is parked in the
 gate while drying

A gear that turns the spool (gear_rotates_spool) only rotated empty gates: retracting a
parked filament every interval would end up pulling it out of the gear. With
heater_rotate_loaded_travel set, a drying cycle with ROTATE=1 also turns the spools
whose filament is parked in the gate, by moving it back and forth between the park and
that far behind it in heater_rotate_distance steps. It never moves forward: on units
whose gates merge into a shared path (QIDI Box) the parked tip sits just short of the
merge, and another filament may be loaded through it.

Not while printing or while the MMU is busy, and never the gate loaded in the
toolhead. The positions are saved (mmu_state_drying_sweep) and only forgotten when
Happy Hare homes that gate again (new mmu:gate_homed event), so a restart or an
interrupted cycle can't add offsets up. Stopping the cycle returns each filament to
its park; one left behind it is harmless as the next load homes to the gate sensor.
Default 0: only empty gates turn, as before.
